Patch 2064: the per-draw fragment constants of patch 2056 cover programs with up to 128 inline constants (was 64).

Programs with more than 64 constants kept the old literal path, so their constants were baked in when the program was
first compiled and every later draw with the same code used them. J-Stars draws its character materials with programs
of about 70 constants and copies them per draw with the material's own values: skin and cloth took the first material's
values, so Goku's and Toriko's skin came out dark brown, Luffy's shirt maroon, Allen's coat near black, and Naruto's
clones and Goku's Victory Burst colours changed with whatever was drawn first. The b1 slot grows from 1280 to 2304
bytes per draw (FP_K_MAX).

Tested (US disc, quick Free Battle route, intro cards every 4 s, against RPCS3 screenshots of the same match): Luffy,
Goku and Toriko skin and clothes match RPCS3; Free Battle 29.99 flips/s (bench/fix/2026-11-09_1448-fpk128).

